  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result so far at 0.619 acc, and avgpool clearly outperforms transformer aggregation (0.619 vs 0.579). However, all multimodal results to date used concat fusion; the effect of weighted fusion is entirely untested. Question: config_019 is a single-variable change from config_018 (concat → weighted fusion), cleanly isolating whether learned modality weighting can improve upon simple concatenation in the best-performing setup. Why this is the best next experiment: it is the lowest-risk, highest-information-value exploitation of the current best configuration. If weighted fusion helps, we immediately have a better config and a new productive axis; if it does not, we rule out fusion as a lever and can confidently pivot to testing a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or learned RNA encoder (SCVI/scGPT) in subsequent experiments, avoiding wasted budget on a dimension that does not matter."
